-- C29 example: near-well salt precipitation by dry-out (TOUGH3 EWASG-type physics in the black-oil engine).
-- A brine aquifer (200 kg/m3 NaCl, 150 C) receives dry gas at the left end; a water producer at the right end keeps the
-- pressure. Gas entering the water-bearing cells evaporates water (vapour capacity from the saturation pressure at 150 C),
-- the brine concentrates above the solubility (317 kg/m3) and halite precipitates; permeability follows the Verma & Pruess
-- tubes-in-series model (phiR 0.8, Gamma 0.8). Results: 3D arrays SSALT (solid fraction of the pore volume) and KSALT
-- (permeability factor), injector BHP rising as the near-well permeability drops. OPM Flow ignores the RESSIM SALT line
-- (it then runs the same case without salt).
-- Expected: the injector cell dries out by day ~70 (Sw 0.002), solid salt 2.8 % of the pore volume, permeability factor 0.76;
-- about 32 m3 of water evaporated in total. Runs in under a second.
RUNSPEC
TITLE
Salt precipitation by dry-out around a gas injector (C29)
DIMENS
 40 1 1 /
OIL
WATER
GAS
METRIC
TABDIMS
 1 1 20 20 /
WELLDIMS
 2 1 1 2 /
START
 1 JAN 2025 /
GRID
DX
 10*1 30*5 /
DY
 40*50 /
DZ
 40*10 /
TOPS
 40*1500 /
PORO
 40*0.2 /
PERMX
 40*200 /
PERMY
 40*200 /
PERMZ
 40*20 /
-- RESSIM: SALT 200 317 2165 0.8 0.8 150 0
PROPS
PVDO
 100 1.10 1.0
 300 1.08 1.1 /
PVTW
 150 1.0 4e-5 0.4 0 /
PVDG
 50  0.0240 0.015
 150 0.0080 0.019
 300 0.0042 0.026 /
DENSITY
 800 1100 0.8 /
ROCK
 150 4e-5 /
SWOF
 0.2 0 1 0
 0.6 0.25 0.1 0
 1.0 1 0 0 /
SGOF
 0    0    1 0
 0.2  0.05 0.4 0
 0.5  0.35 0.05 0
 0.8  0.8  0 0 /
SOLUTION
EQUIL
 1505 150 1000 0 900 0 /
SCHEDULE
WELSPECS
 INJ G 1 1 1505 GAS /
 PRD G 40 1 1505 WATER /
/
COMPDAT
 INJ 1 1 1 1 OPEN 1* 1* 0.15 /
 PRD 40 1 1 1 OPEN 1* 1* 0.15 /
/
WCONINJE
 INJ GAS OPEN RATE 50000 1* 400 /
/
WCONPROD
 PRD OPEN BHP 5* 150 /
/
TSTEP
 10*3 16*20 /
END
